      "side": 1,
      "message": "The reason we do an ioremap for the IOMMU\u0027s MMIO and read the cap/ecap from the hardware is that, the drhd-\u003eiommu-\u003ecap/ecap is already modified by pkvm_update_iommu_virtual_caps() at this point, e.g. the nested ecap is removed by this function. I guess with this change, even dmar2 also has the warning \"nested translation not supported\" below, which is expected only for dmar0 and dmar1.\n\nIf this is true, then it is better to make the pkvm hypervisor to read the cap/ecap from the hardware rather than getting from the info-\u003ecap/ecap (the change in hyp/iommu.c)",
      "revId": "ffd1c18811a50d7d96a4b9198f4d2a44265d85f0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f7f55095_c4f5557f",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/vmx/pkvm/pkvm_host.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 199,
      "author": {
        "id": 4168684
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-04T01:59:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the ecap/ecap is read from the HW again, the ECAP.DT needs to be updated for iommu* based on the SATC parsed entries. Those SATC entries \u0027dmar_satc_units\u0027 are static to the driver hence can\u0027t be accessed in the PKVM hypervisor. Thus copying the cap/ecap from the host here.\nTo avoid the warning for dmar2, the hypervisor can still read from HW and check for NEST and but the copy to pkvm_iommu_inf-\u003ecap/ecap should be from the host iommu ecap/ecap. Does that sound okay?",
      "parentUuid": "56f2e856_fce46a3d",
      "revId": "ffd1c18811a50d7d96a4b9198f4d2a44265d85f0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "62677363_2d8dbcfd",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/vmx/pkvm/pkvm_host.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 199,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015280
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-04T02:21:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I feel that, the key point implemented by this patch is to set the DT bit in IOMMU\u0027s ecap if the SATC has ATC_REQUIRED flag. And then in the hyp/iommu.c the device iotlb enabling is based on whether the DT bit is set or not. That is why you don\u0027t want to read from hardware directly, as the value from the hardware is not based on the SATC parsing result.\n\nHowever, with this patch, for example, if an IOMMU contains two devices, device A is described by the SATC, but the device B is not. Then seems this patch will set the DT bit for this IOMMU. And the pkvm hypervisor will enable device iotlb for both device A and device B, but in fact, we only want the device A to have device iotlb as device B is not described in the SATC.",
      "parentUuid": "f7f55095_c4f5557f",
      "revId": "ffd1c18811a50d7d96a4b9198f4d2a44265d85f0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "732d7fd6_5cde1f48",
        "filename": "drivers/iommu/intel/iommu.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 3064,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015280
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-04T01:11:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Shall the ATC_REQUIRED flag being checked here? My understanding is that, if ATC_REQUIRED flag is not set, it means we don\u0027t need to enable the device IOTLB for the devices covered by this STAC table (suppose we don\u0027t need to look into the device scope to query the ATC_REQUIRED for each device). Is this a correct understanding?\n\nAnother question is that, for an IOMMU, if one of its device is listed in the SATC, then this IOMMU will be marked have device iotlb ecap, then the pkvm hypervisor will not clear the DTE from the context entry for any device in this IOMMU. This sounds like an overfit?",
      "revId": "ffd1c18811a50d7d96a4b9198f4d2a44265d85f0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
